% Commodes: LCD L33736 and its Policy Article A52461 (DME MACs). A policy
% program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery,
% benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a claim for a
% commode chair — stationary (E0163), with detachable arms (E0165), extra
% wide/heavy duty (E0168), with seat lift mechanism (E0170, E0171) — or its
% pail or pan (E0167) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the beneficiary is
% "physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities", which the
% LCD says occurs in three situations (confined to a single room; confined to
% one level of the home with no toilet on that level; confined to the home
% with no toilet facilities in it); the detachable arms feature necessary;
% a weight of 300 pounds or more for the extra wide/heavy duty chair; the
% seat lift criteria for a commode with seat lift mechanism. The footrest
% (E0175, "not medical in nature") and the raised toilet seat (E0244,
% noncovered) are within the policy's scope and outside the benefit: no
% rule places them in a benefit category. A commode chair "used as a raised
% toilet seat by positioning it over the toilet" is noncovered too (the
% Policy Article): what the record states about the use is a scenario fact.
%
% How the criteria are read. The three situations of incapacity are what
% the record states — confinement, and the absence of a toilet — as
% scenario facts, positive statements of the record (the absence of a
% toilet is stated, not presumed from silence). The detachable arms
% criterion is a clinical judgment: the judged template of dmepos.le, "the
% finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with who found it and
% why. The seat lift criteria are those of LCD L33801 ("see Local Coverage
% Determination (LCD) and Policy Article on Seat Lift Mechanisms"), read
% here as its four clinical findings, the ones seat_lifts.le reads under
% the same names. The findings this policy reads, and the criterion each
% stands for:
%   detachable arms necessary (E0165: necessary to facilitate transferring
%   the beneficiary, or a body configuration that requires extra width —
%   ONE finding with the alternatives as its reasons); qualifying seat lift
%   diagnosis, seat lift part of course of treatment, completely incapable
%   of standing from any chair, able to ambulate once standing (E0170,
%   E0171: the seat lift mechanism's criteria, seat_lifts.le).
% The weight is what the record states, in pounds. The LCD's threshold for
% E0168 is stated twice, "300 pounds or more" and, in the denial, "does not
% weigh more than 300 pounds": the coverage statement is followed (300
% qualifies).
%
% Not modelled: the KX/GA/GY/GZ modifiers (billing); the Column I/Column II
% bundling of the pail (E0167) and the seat lift mechanism (E0627, E0629)
% billed with a commode; the toilet seat lift mechanism (E0172) and the
% bidets (A9270), both noncovered as not primarily medical in nature — the
% codes are the seat lift policy's (seat_lifts.le). The Policy Article's
% requirement that "the diagnosis code that justifies the need for these
% items must be included on the claim" names no code list (the article has
% no ICD-10 table): it is not modelled, and the policy declares no
% documentation requirements of its own.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* is confined to a single room; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is confined to one level of the home; undefined.
    the level of the home to which *a beneficiary* is confined has no toilet; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is confined to the home; undefined.
    the home of *a beneficiary* has no toilet facilities; undefined.
    *an item* is used as a raised toilet seat positioned over the toilet; undefined.
    % the knowledge base
    commode code *a code* is noncovered by the Policy Article.
    % derived
    *an item* is a commode chair.
    *an item* is provided as a commode.
    *a beneficiary* is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities.
    *an item* meets the commode coverage criteria for *a beneficiary*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the seat lift criteria for a commode.

the knowledge base commodes includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base commodes includes:

LCD L33736 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33736".
the text of LCD L33736 is at "sources/lcd/L33736.txt".
Policy Article A52461 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52461".
the text of Policy Article A52461 is at "sources/article/A52461.txt".

% What a commode chair is: the commodes the Policy Article's modifier rules
% name.
rule commodes_commode_chair with provenance Policy Article A52461,
        confer "For commodes (E0163, E0165, E0168, E0170, and E0171) not used as a raised toilet seat, the KX modifier must be added to the code only if all of the coverage criteria as described in the Coverage Indication, Limitations and/or Medical Necessity section of the related LCD have been met":
an item is a commode chair
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0163", "E0165", "E0168", "E0170", "E0171"].

% A commode chair provided as a commode, not as a raised toilet seat.
rule commodes_not_raised_seat with provenance Policy Article A52461,
        confer "a commode chair that is used as a raised toilet seat by positioning it over the toilet is also noncovered":
an item is provided as a commode
    if the item is a commode chair
    and it is not the case that
        the item is used as a raised toilet seat positioned over the toilet.

% The codes the Policy Article places outside the benefit.
commode code "E0175" is noncovered by the Policy Article,
    as stated in Policy Article A52461, confer "A footrest (E0175) is non-covered because it is not medical in nature".
commode code "E0244" is noncovered by the Policy Article,
    as stated in Policy Article A52461, confer "A raised toilet seat (E0244) is noncovered".

section applicability is:

commodes has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the commode chairs, the pail or pan, the
% footrest and the raised toilet seat.
rule commodes_codes with provenance Policy Article A52461,
        confer "Commodes are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is commodes
    if the code is in ["E0163", "E0165", "E0167", "E0168", "E0170", "E0171", "E0175", "E0244"].

% Their benefit: durable medical equipment, except the footrest and the
% raised toilet seat.
rule commodes_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52461,
        confer "Commodes are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is commodes
    and it is not the case that
        commode code the code is noncovered by the Policy Article.

section question is:

% A commode chair: the beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing
% regular toilet facilities, and the chair's own criteria are met.
rule commodes_covered with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "A commode is covered when the beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is provided as a commode
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities
    and the item meets the commode coverage criteria for the beneficiary.

% The three situations of incapacity.
rule commodes_single_room with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "The beneficiary is confined to a single room":
a beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities
    if the beneficiary is confined to a single room.

rule commodes_one_level with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "The beneficiary is confined to one level of the home environment and there is no toilet on that level":
a beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities
    if the beneficiary is confined to one level of the home
    and the level of the home to which the beneficiary is confined has no toilet.

rule commodes_home_without_toilet with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "The beneficiary is confined to the home and there are no toilet facilities in the home":
a beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities
    if the beneficiary is confined to the home
    and the home of the beneficiary has no toilet facilities.

% The chair's own criteria: none for the stationary commode chair.
rule commodes_stationary with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "A commode is covered when the beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities":
an item meets the commode coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0163".

% Detachable arms: the finding.
rule commodes_detachable_arms with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "A commode chair with detachable arms (E0165) is covered if the detachable arms feature is necessary to facilitate transferring the beneficiary or if the beneficiary has a body configuration that requires extra width":
an item meets the commode coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0165"
    and the finding detachable arms necessary about the beneficiary is established.

% Extra wide/heavy duty: a weight of 300 pounds or more.
rule commodes_heavy_duty with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "An extra wide/heavy duty commode chair (E0168) is covered for a beneficiary who weighs 300 pounds or more":
an item meets the commode coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0168"
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number >= 300.

% With seat lift mechanism: the seat lift criteria.
rule commodes_seat_lift with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "Commode chair with seat lift mechanism (E0170, E0171) is covered if the beneficiary has medical necessity for a commode and meets the coverage criteria for a seat lift mechanism":
an item meets the commode coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0170", "E0171"]
    and the beneficiary meets the seat lift criteria for a commode.

% The seat lift criteria of LCD L33801, as its four clinical findings
% (seat_lifts.le reads the same findings for the mechanism itself).
rule commodes_seat_lift_criteria with provenance LCD L33736,
        confer "meets the coverage criteria for a seat lift mechanism (see Local Coverage Determination (LCD) and Policy Article on Seat Lift Mechanisms)":
a beneficiary meets the seat lift criteria for a commode
    if the finding qualifying seat lift diagnosis about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding seat lift part of course of treatment about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding completely incapable of standing from any chair about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding able to ambulate once standing about the beneficiary is established.

% The pail or pan (E0167), billed apart from the chair it is provided with
% (the Policy Article's Column II bundling), is read as an accessory of a
% commode chair that meets the coverage criteria — a device of this model:
% the LCD states no criterion for it.
rule commodes_pail:
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0167"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is provided as a commode
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary is physically incapable of utilizing regular toilet facilities
    and the device meets the commode coverage criteria for the beneficiary.
